<Layouts.app flash={@flash} current_scope={@current_scope}>
  <div class="card mx-auto max-w-3xl">
    <.legal_draft_notice>
      Consumer refund rights for cancelled/delayed travel are regulated in
      many jurisdictions (e.g. EU261 in the EU/UK, DOT rules in the US) and
      can override what a business's own policy says — including the cutoff
      windows and fees below, which are placeholders.
    </.legal_draft_notice>

    <h2 class="mt-6 text-3xl font-bold">Refund &amp; Cancellation Policy</h2>
    <p class="mt-1 text-center text-sm text-(--text-muted)">Last updated: August 10, 2026</p>

    <h3 class="mt-6 text-xl font-semibold">1. Cancelling a Booking</h3>
    <p class="mt-2">
      You can cancel any upcoming, confirmed booking yourself from <.link
        href="/account"
        class="text-brand-600 underline hover:text-brand-700 dark:text-brand-400"
      >My Bookings</.link>.
      Cancelling releases your seat immediately and refunds its price to the
      original payment method used at checkout.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-6 text-xl font-semibold">2. What Gets Refunded</h3>
    <p class="mt-2">
      If you booked multiple seats in one order and cancel only one, only that
      seat's price is refunded — the rest of the order is unaffected. [Add any
      cancellation fee or refund-percentage schedule here, e.g. "full refund
      up to 24 hours before departure, 50% within 24 hours, non-refundable
      after departure" — none is currently enforced by the system.]
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-6 text-xl font-semibold">3. Refund Timing</h3>
    <p class="mt-2">
      Refunds are issued to your original payment method immediately when you
      cancel. Your bank or card issuer may take several business days to
      reflect the refund in your account or statement — that delay happens on
      their end, not ours.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-6 text-xl font-semibold">4. If Checkout Fails</h3>
    <p class="mt-2">
      If your payment succeeds but a seat you selected was claimed by another
      passenger in the moments before your payment was confirmed, your entire
      payment is refunded automatically and no booking is created. You do not
      need to request this — it happens as part of completing checkout.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-6 text-xl font-semibold">5. If a Refund Doesn't Go Through</h3>
    <p class="mt-2">
      In rare cases a refund attempt can fail on the payment processor's side.
      Your cancellation still takes effect (your seat is released either way);
      if you don't see your refund within a reasonable time, contact us via
      <.link
        href="/contact"
        class="text-brand-600 underline hover:text-brand-700 dark:text-brand-400"
      >Contact Us</.link>
      with your confirmation code.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-6 text-xl font-semibold">6. Changes to This Policy</h3>
    <p class="mt-2">
      We may update this policy from time to time. Material changes will be
      reflected by updating the date at the top of this page.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layouts.app>
